#: templates/report.html.j2:270
msgid "What CR_eff means — and what it does not"
msgstr "What CR_eff means — and what it does not"

#: templates/report.html.j2:272
msgid ""
"<b>CR_eff is an approach, not a target value.</b> It converts the basal "
"the loop pushed in\n"
"    into an \"effectively used\" ratio: <code>CR_eff = CHO / (bolus + "
"loop extra basal)</code>."
msgstr ""
"<b>CR_eff is an approach, not a target value.</b> It converts the basal "
"the loop pushed in\n"
"    into an \"effectively used\" ratio: <code>CR_eff = CHO / (bolus + "
"loop extra basal)</code>."

#: templates/report.html.j2:274
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Example %(label)s: %(cho)s g on\n"
"    (%(bol)s U bolus + %(loop)s U loop) ≈ <b>%(cre)s</b>\n"
"    instead of the configured ratio."
msgstr ""
"Example %(label)s: %(cho)s g on\n"
"    (%(bol)s U bolus + %(loop)s U loop) ≈ <b>%(cre)s</b>\n"
"    instead of the configured ratio."

#: templates/report.html.j2:276
#, python-format
msgid ""
"And even then the BG at\n"
"    %(w)s is still <b>%(d4)s %(unit)s</b> above baseline — the loop-"
"boosted amount\n"
"    was not enough within the window. <b>CR_eff is a lower bound "
"here</b>: the actually needed CR\n"
"    is even tighter (roughly: an additional ~Δ/ISF units)."
msgstr ""
"And even then the BG at\n"
"    %(w)s is still <b>%(d4)s %(unit)s</b> above baseline — the loop-"
"boosted amount\n"
"    was not enough within the window. <b>CR_eff is a lower bound "
"here</b>: the actually needed CR\n"
"    is even tighter (roughly: an additional ~Δ/ISF units)."

#: templates/report.html.j2:280
msgid ""
"<b>Meant as:</b> direction and order of magnitude — <b>not</b> an exact "
"pump setting.\n"
"    Approximation (loop extra fully attributed to the meal; "
"corrections/exercise/adaptation possible).\n"
"    Small step with the team; re-check after ~1–2 weeks."
msgstr ""
"<b>Meant as:</b> direction and order of magnitude — <b>not</b> an exact "
"pump setting.\n"
"    Approximation (loop extra fully attributed to the meal; "
"corrections/exercise/adaptation possible).\n"
"    Small step with the team; re-check after ~1–2 weeks."

