" over 25 min in the window (excluded from the clean median when enough "
"other meals exist)."

#: templates/report.html.j2:300
msgid "Interpretation &amp; limitations"
msgstr "Interpretation &amp; limitations"

#: templates/report.html.j2:303
msgid ""
"This is <b>decision evidence for the diabetes care team</b>, not a dosing"
" instruction."
msgstr ""
"This is <b>decision evidence for the diabetes care team</b>, not a dosing"
" instruction."

#: templates/report.html.j2:305
msgid ""
"• Under CamAPS Auto Mode the loop compensates continuously; that is "
"exactly why the loop extra\n"
"      basal is the meaningful signal. The algorithm adapts over days and "
"can partly smooth out\n"
"      longer-standing misconfigurations."
msgstr ""
"• Under CamAPS Auto Mode the loop compensates continuously; that is "
"exactly why the loop extra\n"
"      basal is the meaningful signal. The algorithm adapts over days and "
"can partly smooth out\n"
"      longer-standing misconfigurations."

#: templates/report.html.j2:308
msgid ""
"• Confounders (fat/protein, exercise, split boluses, overlapping meals) "
"are dampened by medians,\n"
"      not eliminated; slots with few \"clean\" meals"
msgstr ""
"• Confounders (fat/protein, exercise, split boluses, overlapping meals) "
"are dampened by medians,\n"
"      not eliminated; slots with few \"clean\" meals"

#: templates/report.html.j2:309
msgid "are less certain."
msgstr "are less certain."

#: templates/report.html.j2:310
msgid ""
"• <b>Boost / Ease-off</b> are not present in the Glooko CSV export and "
"cannot be detected automatically.\n"
"      If either mode is active somewhere in the post-meal window, loop "
"extra basal and CR signals can be\n"
"      distorted — interpret such windows with the care team; exclude them"
" mentally from CR conclusions if known."
msgstr ""
"• <b>Boost / Ease-off</b> are not present in the Glooko CSV export and "
"cannot be detected automatically.\n"
"      If either mode is active somewhere in the post-meal window, loop "
"extra basal and CR signals can be\n"
"      distorted — interpret such windows with the care team; exclude them"
" mentally from CR conclusions if known."

#: templates/report.html.j2:313
msgid ""
"• The fasting basal as a reference (mean of the nights) assumes meal"
"-/correction-free nights 00:00–06:00."
msgstr ""
"• The fasting basal as a reference (mean of the nights) assumes meal"
"-/correction-free nights 00:00–06:00."

#: templates/report.html.j2:314
msgid ""
"• <b>Stability</b> (shown next to a verdict where enough meals on enough "
"separate days\n"
"      exist) resamples whole recorded days with replacement and re-runs "
"the same rule. It states how\n"
"      sensitive the verdict is to <b>which meals happened to be "
"recorded</b> — not how likely the carb\n"
"      ratio is correct, and not a confidence interval for a true value. A"
" verdict that flips under\n"
"      resampling rests on a few individual meals; one that holds does not"
" become clinically right by\n"
"      that alone. The thresholds for high/moderate/low are heuristic."
msgstr ""
"• <b>Stability</b> (shown next to a verdict where enough meals on enough "
"separate days\n"
"      exist) resamples whole recorded days with replacement and re-runs "
"the same rule. It states how\n"
"      sensitive the verdict is to <b>which meals happened to be "
"recorded</b> — not how likely the carb\n"
"      ratio is correct, and not a confidence interval for a true value. A"
" verdict that flips under\n"
"      resampling rests on a few individual meals; one that holds does not"
" become clinically right by\n"
"      that alone. The thresholds for high/moderate/low are heuristic."

